  "id": "Compound::DB01161 - Gene::6336",
  "verbalization": "Chloroprocaine, a local anesthetic, is implicated in the interaction with Scn10a through a shared pathway involving anesthetic agents. The evidence suggests that Chloroprocaine, as part of the local anesthetic class, binds to Scn10a, with both Chloroprocaine and Lidocaine contributing to the mechanism of action. This binding is supported by multiple paths, which highlight the role of anesthetic agents in modulating neuronal activity through Scn10a. The lowest common ancestors of Chloroprocaine and Lidocaine point to the Anesthetic Agent category, reinforcing the connection between these compounds and the target. The mechanism of action appears to involve the modulation of ion channels, with Scn10a likely playing a role in the depolarization and repolarization of neuronal membranes. The evidence is consistent with a direct interaction between Chloroprocaine and Scn10a, supported by the inclusion of both compounds in the same anesthetic class and their shared binding to the target. The integration of these pathways suggests a plausible mechanism by which Chloroprocaine exerts its effects on Scn10a, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
